{"hash":"282bea3b959fc56d","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":85.135,"said":"As you go down, listen. The Shiva Purana tells of a boy named Bhima, who grew up on these Sahya mountains with his mother, a rakshasi. One day he asked her, ‘Who was my father? Why are we alone?’ She told him: your father was Kumbhakarna, the giant brother of Lanka’s king, and he was killed by Rama in the war of Lanka. Bhima’s grief turned to rage. He went into the forest and, the Purana says, stood for a thousand years on one foot with his arms raised in penance, until Brahma, the Creator, granted him strength beyond all others. Then Bhima swept across the world. He defeated the gods. He seized the kingdom of Kamarupa, far to the east, and threw its king, Sudakshina, into chains. But in his prison the king did a quiet, stubborn thing. He shaped a linga out of earth and, with his queen beside him, worshipped Shiva every day. When Bhima heard of it, he came with his sword drawn. What happened next is why this place is holy. Keep going, all the way down. The tank behind the temple is waiting.\n\nDid you know? About two kilometres into the forest is Gupt Bhimashankar, where a small waterfall of the young Bhima pours without pause onto a Shivalinga.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1005},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1021,"end":1161}],"words":[[0.098,0.192,0,2],[0.302,0.132,3,6],[0.447,0.18,7,9],[0.639,0.421,10,14],[1.216,0.565,16,22],[2.608,0.12,24,27],[2.74,0.349,28,33],[3.101,0.481,34,40],[3.594,0.3,41,46],[3.906,0.12,47,49],[4.038,0.06,50,51],[4.111,0.325,52,55],[4.447,0.312,56,61],[4.772,0.457,62,67],[5.421,0.096,69,72],[5.529,0.288,73,77],[5.829,0.192,78,80],[6.034,0.156,81,83],[6.202,0.24,84,89],[6.454,0.312,90,95],[6.779,0.625,96,105],[7.416,0.18,106,110],[7.608,0.168,111,114],[7.788,0.445,115,121],[8.45,0.084,123,124],[8.546,0.745,125,133],[10.18,0.288,135,138],[10.481,0.204,139,142],[10.697,0.168,143,145],[10.877,0.325,146,151],[11.214,0.276,152,155],[11